 naming them, so the remaining 8 regions have no rows. Named regions sum to 110 of the national 171. Zambezi matched to geoBoundaries 'Caprivi' (the region's name before 2013)."},"newera_gbv_2019_20":{"name":"Police record nearly 6 000 GBV cases","publisher":"New Era (news, Nampa copy), citing NamPol GBV unit head Deputy Commissioner Johanna Situde","url":"https://neweralive.na/?p=155194","licence":"no licence stated (news article; figures are police statistics quoted by the outlet)","years":"September 2019 - September 2020","notes":"Last-resort source under RETRY2 route 4. These are murder cases within the police gender-based-violence case count, not all murders. Only five regions named; they sum to 50 of 74. Published 26 October 2020."}},"dict":{"b":["Total"],"m":["Murder cases reported to police, as reported by The Namibian, citing Namibian Police Inspector-General Joseph Shikongo","Gender-based-violence murder cases reported to police (NamPol GBV unit), as reported by New Era/Nampa, citing Deputy Commissioner Johanna Situde"],"u":["count"],"s":["namibian_h1_2024","newera_gbv_2019_20"],"c":["2024 H1 (1 Jan-30 Jun)","Sep 2019-Sep 2020"]},"problems":"Searched Namibia Statistics Agency and NAMPOL. Regional crime figures appear only in news (New Era, The Namibian, NAMPA) quoting police; no official downloadable regional murder table found. RETRY 17 Oct: tried cause-of-death route. The NSA/MoHSS 'Report on Mortality and Causes of Deaths in Namibia 2016-2017' (raw/Causes_of_Death_Report_2016-2017.pdf, from https://www.afro.who.int/sites/default/files/2021-11/Causes_of_Death_Report_0.pdf) gives homicide deaths (73 in 2016, 71 in 2017) and leading assault ICD codes nationally only; its regional breakdowns are for broad groups (injuries as a whole, in percentage charts), not homicide. Searches for NAMPOL annual crime statistics found only press reports (New Era, Namibian Sun) quoting police; HDX has no Namibian crime dataset; web.archive.org unreachable from the shell. The 2018-2021 causes-of-death report (listed on GHDx) was not checked. THIRD PASS 17 Oct: route 4 (news quoting police). Found two partial regional sets: The Namibian 15 Aug 2024 (Jan-Jun 2024 murder cases, 6 named regions + national 171) and New Era 26 Oct 2020 (GBV-related murder cases Sep 2019-Sep 2020, 5 named regions + national 74). Also checked: New Era ?p=325931 (17 Dec 2021, national 308 murders, no regions), New Era ?p=296051, The Namibian 'Crimes skyrocketing' and Namibian Sun 2024-07-24 (2023/24 total crime 110,551 and regional shares of all crime, no murder by region). The 2018-2021 causes-of-death report was not checked this pass either.","unmatched":0,"shapes":{"shapes_ADM1.geojson":{"source":"geoBoundaries gbOpen NAM ADM1","url":"https://github.com/wmgeolab/geoBoundaries/raw/9469f09/releaseData/gbOpen/NAM/ADM1/geoBoundaries-NAM-ADM1_simplified.geojson","licence":"CC BY 4.0","notes":"Pre-2013 regions: 'Kavango' (now Kavango East and Kavango West) and 'Caprivi' (renamed Zambezi); also contains a feature named 'Cunene' besides 'Kunene' (not used)."}}}